<Base title="Privacy and optional analytics" description="How Acquisition Companion handles optional analytics, local progress, and search." type="About"><Crumbs items={[{title:'Privacy'}]}/><article class="narrow"><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">Your choice</p><h1>Privacy and analytics.</h1></header><div class="prose"><p>Acquisition Companion is free to read without an account. Lesson progress and your analytics choice are saved in this browser. Site search runs locally in your browser.</p><h2>Optional Google Analytics</h2><p>If you choose “Allow analytics,” the site loads Google Analytics to understand aggregate site usage. It can record page views, course starts, completed lessons, searches, and clicks to original YouTube sources. Search events include the term only when it exactly matches a short list of educational topics; other searches are recorded without the text. We do not send transcript text to Google.</p><p>You can choose “No thanks” and use the entire site. Google Analytics does not load before consent or after a decline. No advertising, remarketing, or advertising personalization is enabled.</p><p>Use <strong>Analytics preferences</strong> in the footer to change your choice. Changing from allow to decline reloads the page to stop the active analytics script. Following an external source link takes you to that site’s own privacy practices.</p></div></article></Base>
